# XSH fchown()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.fchown.001
anchor     functions/fchown.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       With appropriate privileges, fchown(fd, 65534, 65533) on a
           descriptor open on f returns 0 and f then has those IDs; (uid_t)-1
           and (gid_t)-1 leave the corresponding ID alone.
needs      root
test       t/001-sets-ids.c

assertion  XSH.fchown.002
anchor     functions/fchown.html#ERRORS/EPERM
class      required
since      1988
says       A process without appropriate privileges can fchown() a file it
           owns to (uid_t)-1 and its effective group ID, and cannot give it
           to another user (EPERM).
test       t/002-own-group.c

assertion  XSH.fchown.003
anchor     functions/fchown.html#ERRORS/EPERM
class      required
since      1988
says       For a process without appropriate privileges, fchown() of a file it
           does not own, open for reading, to (uid_t)-1 and its own group,
           fails with EPERM.
needs      root
test       t/003-not-owner.c

assertion  XSH.fchown.004
anchor     functions/fchown.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      1988
says       fchown() of a descriptor that is not open fails with EBADF.
test       t/004-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.fchown.005
anchor     functions/chown.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       After fchown(fd, uid, gid) with the file's own IDs, fstat() reports a
           later st_ctim (the test calls it every 10 ms for up to 3 s until
           it moves).
timeout    20
test       t/005-ctime.c
